  "instructions": {
    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "content": [
          "## Visualization hint (machine-readable)\n",
          "\n",
          "After answering any question whose result is a SQL table, append ONE fenced\n",
          "JSON code block as the LAST element of your response. Use exactly this schema\n",
          "and these field names. This block is parsed by an application, not read by a\n",
          "human — never wrap it in explanation, never omit it.\n",
          "\n",
          "```json\n",
          "{\n",
          "  \"viz\": {\n",
          "    \"chart_type\": \"bar | line | area | point | arc | table\",\n",
          "    \"x\":     { \"field\": \"<exact result column name>\", \"type\": \"nominal | ordinal | quantitative | temporal\" },\n",
          "    \"y\":     { \"field\": \"<exact result column name>\", \"type\": \"quantitative | nominal | temporal\", \"aggregate\": \"sum | mean | count | none\" },\n",
          "    \"color\": { \"field\": \"<exact result column name or null>\", \"type\": \"nominal | ordinal | quantitative\" },\n",
          "    \"title\": \"<short chart title>\",\n",
          "    \"reason\": \"<one short sentence on why this chart fits>\"\n",
          "  }\n",
          "}\n",
          "```\n",
          "\n",
          "Rules for the viz block:\n",
          "- x.field, y.field, and color.field MUST be exact, case-sensitive column names\n",
          "  from the SQL result. Never invent a field that is not in the result.\n",
          "- Pick chart_type from the data shape:\n",
          "  - a date/time column on x  -> \"line\" (or \"area\" for cumulative totals)\n",
          "  - one categorical dimension + one measure -> \"bar\"\n",
          "  - two numeric measures -> \"point\" (scatter)\n",
          "  - one categorical split of a single total -> \"arc\" (pie)\n",
          "  - a single scalar value, or more than two dimensions, or no sensible\n",
          "    encoding -> \"table\", and set x/y/color fields to null.\n",
          "- Set color.field to null when there is no grouping/series dimension.\n",
          "- \"type\" must reflect the column: dates/timestamps -> \"temporal\",\n",
          "  numeric measures -> \"quantitative\", text/category -> \"nominal\",\n",
          "  ordered buckets -> \"ordinal\".\n",
          "- Always emit the block even when chart_type is \"table\".\n",
          "\n",
          "## Result size\n",
          "Unless the user explicitly asks for all rows, limit results to the top 100\n",
          "rows (apply LIMIT or an aggregation) so the application stays responsive."
        ],
        "id": "01f16f975aef1f469c25a0ca66bfcb2d"
